# Studio chrome and generation

Do not revert or replace studio/admin chrome (`StudioShell`, `AppHeader`, `PageTabs`, `StudioButton`, `StudioField`, `StudioLogo`). New authenticated screens should compose these, not invent a parallel layout.

Generation is **backgrounded**. The stream is owned by `GenerationProvider` (`app/providers.tsx` → `lib/generation/generation-runtime`). Leaving `/generation` must not abort the job.

- Use `useGeneration()` from `components/app/generation/GenerationProvider`. Do not start a local fetch/stream that dies on unmount.
- Persist progress through the generation runtime (`startGeneration`, `startApply`, `attachToProject`).
- Dashboard and studio headers should keep reflecting an in-flight job.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — page-local stream dies on navigate
useEffect(() => { const c = new AbortController(); fetch("/api/generate", { signal: c.signal }); return () => c.abort(); }, []);

// ✅ GOOD — provider-owned job
const { startGeneration, isJobActive } = useGeneration();
await startGeneration(input);
```
